795609 -3 0 -3 \nC -0.795609 -3 -1.55874 -2.683901 -2.12132 -2.12132 \nC -2.683901 -1.55874 -3 -0.795609 -3 0 \nC -3 0.795609 -2.683901 1.55874 -2.12132 2.12132 \nC -1.55874 2.683901 -0.795609 3 0 3 \nz\n\" id=\"m5ec15a0b19\" style=\"stroke:#000000;\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g clip-path=\"url(#pc4db36c1a7)\">\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"72.673142\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"283.653134\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"115.044144\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"229.726404\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"149.711328\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"193.775251\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"192.08233\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"157.824098\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"149.711328\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"229.726404\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"192.08233\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"211.750828\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"222.897604\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"157.824098\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"222.897604\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"121.872944\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"265.268606\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"85.921791\"></use>\n<use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"311.491518\" xlink:href=\"#m5ec15a0b19\" y=\"85.921791\"></use>\n</g>\n</g>\n<g id=\"line2d_2\">\n<path clip-path=\"url(#pc4db36c1a7)\" d=\"M 53.413596 294.875707 \nL 323.047246 58.747597 \nL 323.047246 58.747597 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n<defs>\n<clipPath id=\"pc4db36c1a7\">\n<rect height=\"347.76\" width=\"349.984478\" x=\"9.867761\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n</clipPath>\n</defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The scatterplot has 10 data points.</li><li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li><li>A line of best fit is shown:<br><ul><li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li><li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br><ul><li>(1 comma 3.3)</li><li>(3 comma 7.0)</li><li>(5 comma 10.8)</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown?</p>","keys":["035e9c26-e0a8-43a7-b3a3-7a6cfab55557"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"7e41a0ce-e619-4ba8-a8cc-6fe60961875e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5013d79e-8bbc-4490-8171-ff40e47109b7","content":"<p><math alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b56ea4f0-be59-43cc-a821-b69e0fc1bd28","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"035e9c26-e0a8-43a7-b3a3-7a6cfab55557","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. A line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the points <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> has a slope of <math alttext=\"StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. The line of best fit shown passes approximately through the points <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 comma 3.3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 7 comma 14.5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14.5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. It follows that the slope of this best fit line is approximately <math alttext=\"StartFraction 14.5 minus 3.3 Over 7 minus 1 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>14.5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3.3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"StartFraction 11.2 Over 6 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>11.2</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>, or approximately <math alttext=\"1.87\"><mn>1.87</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> is closest to the slope of the line of best fit shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"a3419986-a630-4b5b-9c48-62a85f09b32e","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554984,"updateDate":1743430554984}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554984, 1743430554984),
    ($SATQ$90eed2e5$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$026017-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.F.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Inference from sample statistics and margin of error $SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">A city has 50&nbsp;city council members. A reporter polled a random sample of 20&nbsp;city council members and found that 6 of those polled supported a specific bill. Based on the sample, which of the following is the best estimate of the number of city council members in the city who support the bill?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">6</span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">9</span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">15</span>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">30</span>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. Because a random sample of the city council was polled, the proportion of the sample who supported the bill is expected to be approximately equal to the proportion of the total city council who supports the bill. Since 6 of the 20 polled, or 30%, supported the bill, it can be estimated that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/90eed2e5/img_000_3c3eeadc.png" alt="50 times 0 point 3"></span>, or 15, city council members support the bill.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of city council members in the sample who supported the bill. Choice B is incorrect and may result from a computational error. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of city council members in the sample of city council members who were not polled.</p></p>
$SATQ$, true, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"90eed2e5","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"026017-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.F.","skill_desc":"Inference from sample statistics and margin of error ","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A city has 50&nbsp;city council members. A reporter polled a random sample of 20&nbsp;city council members and found that 6 of those polled supported a specific bill. Based on the sample, which of the following is the best estimate of the number of city council members in the city who support the bill?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">6</span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">9</span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">15</span>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<span class=\"choice_cell align:character align_character:. \">30</span>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Because a random sample of the city council was polled, the proportion of the sample who supported the bill is expected to be approximately equal to the proportion of the total city council who supports the bill. Since 6 of the 20 polled, or 30%, supported the bill, it can be estimated that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/90eed2e5/img_000_3c3eeadc.png\" alt=\"50 times 0 point 3\"></span>, or 15, city council members support the bill.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of city council members in the sample who supported the bill. Choice B 