the bill.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the number of city council members in the sample who supported the bill. Choice B is incorrect and may result from a computational error. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of city council members in the sample of city council members who were not polled.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959620,"updateDate":1691007959620,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959620, 1691007959620),
    ($SATQ$9110c120$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$026381-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><p class="standalone_statement style:1 "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9110c120/img_000_7334cb56.png" alt="Data set A consists of 9 data values, each of which is the integer 5.
Data set B consists of 10 data values, nine of which are the integer 5, and one of which is the integer 100."></span></p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Which of the following statements about the means and medians of data set A and data set B is true?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Only the means are different.</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Only the medians are different.</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Both the means and the medians are different.</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Neither the means nor the medians are different.</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. The mean of a data set is the sum of the values divided by the number of values. The mean of data set A is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9110c120/img_001_c699d2fa.png" alt="the fraction 45 over 9"></span>, or 5. The mean of data set B is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9110c120/img_002_8193f0e5.png" alt="the fraction 145 over 10"></span>, or 14.5. Thus, the means are different. The median of a data set is the middle value when the values are ordered from least to greatest. The medians of data sets A and B are both 5. Therefore, the medians are the same, so only the means are different.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
