e fraction 45 over 9\"></span>, or 5. The mean of data set B is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9110c120/img_002_8193f0e5.png\" alt=\"the fraction 145 over 10\"></span>, or 14.5. Thus, the means are different. The median of a data set is the middle value when the values are ordered from least to greatest. The medians of data sets A and B are both 5. Therefore, the medians are the same, so only the means are different.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":3,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959620,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"9110c120","skill_cd":"Q.C.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","createDate":1691007959620,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"026381-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"9558f94f-fe83-4a03-8ffa-cdbeb96508f3","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"026381-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Data set A consists of 9 data values, each of which is the integer 5.\nData set B consists of 10 data values, nine of which are the integer 5, and one of which is the integer 100.\"></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following statements about the means and medians of data set A and data set B is true?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Only the means are different.</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Only the medians are different.</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Both the means and the medians are different.</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">Neither the means nor the medians are different.</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. The mean of a data set is the sum of the values divided by the number of values. The mean of data set A is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 45 over 9\"></span>, or 5. The mean of data set B is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 145 over 10\"></span>, or 14.5. Thus, the means are different. The median of a data set is the middle value when the values are ordered from least to greatest. The medians of data sets A and B are both 5. Therefore, the medians are the same, so only the means are different.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959620,"updateDate":1691007959620}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959620, 1691007959620),
    ($SATQ$912cd125$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$08226-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1" class="stimulus_reference ">
        <div class="passage ">
          <div class="prose style:1 ">
            <p class="passage_para ">For a science project, Anka recorded whether it rained each weekday and weekend day for 12&nbsp;weeks. Her results are summarized in the table below.</p>
            <div class="tcp-bfce9c25-f533-4c4d-9d6d-d0ec1c427561">
              <table class="table_WithBorder tcp-ed9db193-318c-4e20-af8f-a3a23d7c04fc"><caption>Weekday and Weekend Day Rain for 12 Weeks</caption>
                <tbody><tr><td></td>
                    <td>Rain</td>
                    <td>No rain</td>
                    <td>Total</td>
                  </tr><tr><td>Number of weekdays</td>
                    <td class="para_right">12</td>
                    <td class="para_right">48</td>
                    <td class="para_right">60</td>
                  </tr><tr><td>Number of weekend days</td>
                    <td class="para_right">8</td>
                    <td class="para_right">16</td>
                    <td class="para_right">24</td>
                  </tr><tr><td>Total</td>
                    <td class="para_right">20</td>
                    <td class="para_right">64</td>
                    <td class="para_right">84</td>
                  </tr></tbody></table></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">If one of the days on which there was no rain is selected at random, what is the probability the day was a weekend day?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/912cd125/img_000_4a89cf7e.png\" alt=\"the fraction 4 over 21\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/912cd125/img_001_929b687b.png\" alt=\"the fraction 1 over 4\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/912cd125/img_002_d44b10df.png\" alt=\"the fraction 2 over 3\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/912cd125/img_003_86d7be86.png\" alt=\"the fraction 3 over 4\"></span></span>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. There were 64 days with no rain. It was a weekend day for 16 of those 64 days. So 16 out of 64 of the days with no rain were weekend days. Because the day is selected at random, each day has an equal chance of being selected, so the probability is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/912cd125/img_004_8cfc1ba8.png" alt="the fraction 16 over 64, equals the fraction 1 over 4"></span>.<!--[if--><!--[if--><!--[endif]--><!--![endif]--><!--![if--><!--[if--><!--[endif]--><!--[if--><!--[endif]--><!--![endif]--><!--![if--><!--[if--><!--[endif]--><!--[endif]--><!--![endif]--><!--![endif]--><!--![if--><!--![if--><!--![endif]--><!--![endif]--><!--![if--><!--![if--><p>
        <!--[if-->
        <!--[if-->
        <!--[endif]-->
        <!--[endif]-->
        <!--[if-->
        <!--[if-->
        <!--[endif]-->
        <!--[endif]-->
        <!--![endif]-->
        <!--![endif]-->
        <!--![if-->
        <!--![if-->
        <!--![endif]-->
        <!--![endif]-->
        <!--![if-->
        <!--![if-->Choice A is incorrect. It is the probability that a day selected at random from any one of the days during the 12 weeks is a weekend day with no rain. Choice C is incorrect. It is the probability that a day selected at random from the weekend days has no rain. Choice D is incorrect. It is the probability that a day selected at random from the days with no rain is a weekday.</p></p>
