 A is an equation of a line with a positive <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the point with coordinates 0 comma 6 \"></span> and a negative slope, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABcAAAAYCAYAAAARfGZ1AAAACXBIWXMAAA7EAAAOxAGVKw4bAAAABGJhU0UAAAAMyZLetQAAAFhJREFUeNpjYKAMtADxNiB+DsT/oXyqgS9AfAyIp9LCcCYkNtUNZyDWcBEiMBu5hv8nAoeQa7gLEViMXMNpGuYjy/AQJAwyfA0SnyquxYVHwSgYBaOAJgAAQ7AqWC3zu8cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=\" alt=\"negative 1\"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This equation is for a line that has a negative <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept, not a positive <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept. Choices C and D are incorrect and may result from one or more sign errors and from switching the values of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept and the slope in the equation.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959621,"updateDate":1691007959621}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959621, 1691007959621),
    ($SATQ$93724cc6$SATQ$, $SATQ$fc5659d4-90ce-4136-b70e-ac4dd697c151$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;"><math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="21 percent sign"><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of what number?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0c0caab1-60ad-4886-bb4b-c3248f4cd744","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"41307e29-c6b4-41af-8be9-7bb3e69df8b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d3c6f2bc-cfd1-47c9-b2d5-f0831b05c40f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4716046-47c9-4019-b7c6-018580671855","content":"<p><math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e4716046-47c9-4019-b7c6-018580671855"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Let <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represent the number that <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="21 percent sign"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of. It follows that <math alttext="StartFraction 21 Over x EndFraction equals StartFraction 21 Over 100 EndFraction"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mfrac>
			<mn>21</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mfrac>
		<mn>21</mn>
		<mn>100</mn>
	</mfrac>
</mrow>
</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> yields <math alttext="21 equals StartFraction 21 x Over 100 EndFraction"><mrow>
	<mn>21</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mfrac>
			<mrow>
				<mn>21</mn>
				<mi>x</mi>
			</mrow>
			<mn>100</mn>
		</mfrac>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="2,100 equals 21 x"><mrow>
	<mn>2,100</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>21</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="100 equals x"><mrow>
	<mn>100</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="21 percent sign"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext="21 percent sign"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext="21 percent sign"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="0.21"><mn>0.21</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext="21 percent sign"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="42"><mn>42</mn>
</math> is <math alttext="8.82"><mn>8.82</mn>
</math>, not <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"93724cc6","external_id":"fc5659d4-90ce-4136-b70e-ac4dd697c151","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"33aa056b-34e2-4030-a87e-14d5c26ab352","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mrow><mn>21</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of what number?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0c0caab1-60ad-4886-bb4b-c3248f4cd744","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"41307e29-c6b4-41af-8be9-7bb3e69df8b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d3c6f2bc-cfd1-47c9-b2d5-f0831b05c40f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e4716046-47c9-4019-b7c6-018580671855","content":"<p><math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["e4716046-47c9-4019-b7c6-018580671855"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the number that <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 21 Over x EndFraction equals StartFraction 21 Over 100 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t\t<mn>100</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"21 equals StartFraction 21 x Over 100 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mfrac>\n\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>100</mn>\n\t\t</mfrac>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"2,100 equals 21 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>2,100</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>21</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"100 equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>100</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0.21\"><mn>0.21</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect.&nbsp;<math alttext=\"21 percent sign\"><mn>21</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"8.82\"><mn>8.82</mn>\n</math>, not <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357402,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"93724cc6","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1730147357402,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"fc5659d4-90ce-4136-b70e-ac4dd697c151","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"33aa056b-34e2-4030-