<li>The data for the 5 categories are as follows:&nbsp;<br>
<ul>
<li>1: More than halfway above 25 students</li>
<li>2: Less than halfway above 30 students</li>
<li>3: More than halfway above 35 students</li>
<li>4: About halfway above 40 students</li>
<li>5: About halfway above 45 students</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A group of students voted on five after-school activities. The bar graph shows the number of students who voted for each of the five activities. How many students chose activity <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"89f311f5-ce51-4c74-954e-0346f507d843","content":"<p><math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5313894e-7b99-437d-8f92-52980a2a8174","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0d96d458-10d6-44bf-94df-c3914a9c0b23","content":"<p><math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"15ecd9c6-5945-41c5-899b-7eed4b60ea3e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5313894e-7b99-437d-8f92-52980a2a8174"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The height of each bar in the bar graph given represents the number of students that voted for the activity specified at the bottom of the bar. The bar for activity <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> has a height that is between <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math>. In other words, the number of students that chose activity <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> is between <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> students and <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math> students. Of the given choices, <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math> is the only value between <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="40"><mn>40</mn>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math> students chose activity <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the number of students that chose activity <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>, not activity <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"93779b53","external_id":"47edb639-8ebe-471a-ae9d-172195289d2b","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"9a778fd3-9c6c-4114-bb00-a16ccbecf121","uId":"c66c6902-d199-4d64-a3c5-e5e579de1d94","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"354.911\" height=\"284.755\" viewBox=\"0 0 354.911 284.755\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bar graph. The horizontal axis is labeled Activity. 5 data categories are shown. The vertical axis is labeled Number of students. It ranges from 0 to 50 in increments of 5. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"f7af0f02-3425-4747-aecf-af1052fea62e\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><line x1=\"57.974\" y1=\"0.472\" x2=\"57.974\" y2=\"238.209\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"354.439\" y1=\"238.209\" x2=\"57.974\" y2=\"238.209\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"52.304\" y1=\"238.209\" x2=\"63.644\" y2=\"238.209\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"52.304\" y1=\"215.414\" x2=\"63.644\" y2=\"215.414\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.945\"></line><line x1=\"52.304\" y1=\"192.619\" x2=\"63.644\" y2=\"192.619\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=