Fraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It's also given that <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Since&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 100 Over 60 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction b equals c\"><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. If <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, then&nbsp;<math alttext=\"c equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>23</mn>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>p</mi>\n<mn>100</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2,300 Over 6 EndFraction equals p\"><mfrac><mn>2,300</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>. It follows that the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is approximately <math alttext=\"383.33\"><mn>383.33</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext=\"383\"><mn>383</mn>\n</math> is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, and if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554989,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"993000da","skill_cd":"Q.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Percentages","createDate":1743430554989,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"fa595c60-481e-4838-966e-bb53dd5ec839","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"239f9fed-511f-40da-804f-50be52bb1e1d","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The positive number <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mrow><mn>230</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of the number <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of the number <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>. If <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, which of the following is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>?</p>","keys":["d17ee66f-333e-4b12-ae9b-dedb520d5cf6"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"632d7cea-528f-4588-8cce-15e133cabc82","content":"<p><math alttext=\"138\"><mn>138</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"30ad7da0-136d-4eb2-86d4-5e48c485853c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"217\"><mn>217</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"acee6936-7e0f-4444-a9d5-4fdcbd6dba39","content":"<p><math alttext=\"283\"><mn>283</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d17ee66f-333e-4b12-ae9b-dedb520d5cf6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"383\"><mn>383</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It's also given that <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"60 percent sign\"><mn>60</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Since&nbsp;<math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"a equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 230 Over 100 EndFraction b equals StartFraction 60 Over 100 EndFraction c\"><mfrac><mn>230</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>c</mi></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 100 Over 60 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction b equals c\"><mfrac><mn>23</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. If <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, then&nbsp;<math alttext=\"c equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction b\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi></math>. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 23 Over 6 EndFraction equals StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>23</mn>\n<mn>6</mn>\n</mfrac>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mfrac>\n<mi>p</mi>\n<mn>100</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartFraction 2,300 Over 6 EndFraction equals p\"><mfrac><mn>2,300</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>. It follows that the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> is approximately <math alttext=\"383.33\"><mn>383.33</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext=\"383\"><mn>383</mn>\n</math> is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, and if <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>, rather than if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"230 percent sign\"><mn>230</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"p\"><mi>p</mi>\n</math> if <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>, rather than&nbsp;<math alttext=\"p percent sign\"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>.</p>","externalid":"fa595c60-481e-4838-966e-bb53dd5ec839","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1743430554989,"updateDate":1743430554989}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554989, 1743430554989),
    ($SATQ$99550621$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$025315-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Makayla is planning an event in a 5,400-square-foot room. If there should be at least 8 square feet per person, what is the maximum number of people that could attend this event?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">588</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">675</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">15,274</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">43,200</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the event will be in a 5,400-square-foot room and that there should be at least 8 square feet per person. The maximum number of people that could attend the event can be found by dividing the total square feet in the room by the minimum number of square feet needed per person, which gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/99550621/img_000_be3e0515.png" alt="the fraction 5,400 over 8, equals 675"></span>.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect and may result from conceptual or computational errors. Choice D is incorrect and may result from multiplying, rather than dividing, 5,400 by 8.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"99550621","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"025315-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Makayla is planning an event in a 5,400-square-foot room. If there should be at least 8 square feet per person, what is the maximum number of people that could attend this event?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">588</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">675</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">15,274</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">43,200</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the event will be in a 5,400-square-foot room and that there should be at least 8 square feet per person. The maximum number of people that could attend the event can be found by dividing the total square feet in the room by the minimum number of square feet needed per person, which gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/99550621/img_000_be3e0515.png\" alt=\"the fraction 5,400 over 8, equals 675\"></span>.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect and may result from conceptual or computational errors. Choice D is incorrect and may result from multiplying, rather than dividing, 5,400 by 8.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":1,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959618,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"99550621","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1691007959618,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"025315-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"c5d910c7-c52d-4eec-adc5-b8fd11baa9d5","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"025315-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Makayla is planning an event in a 5,400-square-foot room. If there should be at least 8 square feet per person, what is the maximum number of people that could attend this event?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">588</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">675</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">15,274</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">43,200</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the event will be in a 5,400-square-foot room and that there should be at least 8 square feet per person. The maximum number of people that could attend the event can be found by dividing the total square feet in the room by the minimum number of square feet needed per person, which gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction 5,400 over 8, equals 675\"></span>.<p>Choices A and C are incorrect and may result from conceptual or computational errors. Choice D is incorrect and may result from multiplying, rather than dividing, 5,400 by 8.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959618,"updateDate":1691007959618}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959618, 1691007959618),
    ($SATQ$9a144a01$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$031669-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">Which of the following is true about the values of <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_012_3d21008e.png" alt="2 to the x power "></span></span> and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_013_a8e96e50.png" alt="2 x plus 2 "></span></span> for <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_014_8d906565.png" alt="x greater than 0"></span></span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">For all <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_000_8d906565.png\" alt=\"x greater than 0\"></span></span>, it is true that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_001_8efb1355.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span>.</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">For all <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_002_8d906565.png\" alt=\"x greater than 0\"></span></span></span>, it is true that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_003_9eaa3b1a.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span>.</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">There is a constant <span class=\"italic\">c</span> such that if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_004_82b92e34.png\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than c\"></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_005_8efb1355.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span>, but if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_006_9de43665.png\" alt=\"x is greater than c\"></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_007_9eaa3b1a.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span>.</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">There is a constant <span class=\"italic\">c</span> such that if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_008_82b92e34.png\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than c\"></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_009_9eaa3b1a.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span></span>, but if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_010_9de43665.png\" alt=\"x is greater than c\"></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_011_8efb1355.png\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. At <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_015_3f34714f.png" alt="x equals 0"></span>, the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_016_3d21008e.png" alt="2 raised to the x power"></span> is less than the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_017_da06ab59.png" alt="2 x plus 2, where 2 to the 0 power is less than, 2 times 0, plus 2"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_018_da425136.png" alt="1 is less than 2 "></span>. As the value of <span class="italic">x</span> increases, the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_019_3d21008e.png" alt="2 raised to the x power"></span> remains less than the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_020_a8e96e50.png" alt="2 x plus 2"></span> until <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_021_6ec6a793.png" alt="x equals 3"></span>, which is when the two values are equal: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_022_0b72494e.png" alt="2 cubed equals, 2 times 3, plus 2"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_023_3964d6f7.png" alt="8 is equal to 8"></span>. Then, for <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_024_fcb1e8a9.png" alt="x greater than 3"></span>, the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_025_3d21008e.png" alt="2 raised to the x power"></span> is greater than the value of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_026_a8e96e50.png" alt="2 x plus 2"></span>. So there is a constant, 3, such that when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_027_77c73b18.png" alt="0 is less than x, which is less than 3"></span>, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_028_8efb1355.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2"></span>, but when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_029_fcb1e8a9.png" alt="x is greater than 3"></span>, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_030_9eaa3b1a.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_031_9eaa3b1a.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2"></span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_032_fcb1e8a9.png" alt="x is greater than 3"></span>. Choice B is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_033_8efb1355.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2"></span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_034_77c73b18.png" alt="0 is less than x, which is less than 3"></span>. Choice D is incorrect because <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_035_8efb1355.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2"></span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_036_77c73b18.png" alt="0 is less than x, which is less than 3"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_037_9eaa3b1a.png" alt="2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2"></span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_038_fcb1e8a9.png" alt="x is greater than 3"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
