lt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_031_9eaa3b1a.png\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_032_fcb1e8a9.png\" alt=\"x is greater than 3\"></span>. Choice B is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_033_8efb1355.png\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_034_77c73b18.png\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span>. Choice D is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_035_8efb1355.png\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_036_77c73b18.png\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_037_9eaa3b1a.png\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9a144a01/img_038_fcb1e8a9.png\" alt=\"x is greater than 3\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":39,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959627,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"9a144a01","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959627,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"031669-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"2edeac8c-7b7f-4af8-aa83-b033b803c8bd","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"031669-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is true about the values of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power \"></span></span> and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x plus 2 \"></span></span> for <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x greater than 0\"></span></span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">For all <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x greater than 0\"></span></span>, it is true that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span>.</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">For all <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x greater than 0\"></span></span></span>, it is true that <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span>.</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">There is a constant <span class=\"italic\">c</span> such that if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than c\"></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span>, but if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than c\"></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span>.</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">There is a constant <span class=\"italic\">c</span> such that if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than c\"></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is greater than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span></span>, but if <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than c\"></span></span></span>, then <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to the x power, is less than 2 x plus 2\"></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. At <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 0\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power\"></span> is less than the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x plus 2, where 2 to the 0 power is less than, 2 times 0, plus 2\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"1 is less than 2 \"></span>. As the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> increases, the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power\"></span> remains less than the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x plus 2\"></span> until <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 3\"></span>, which is when the two values are equal: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 cubed equals, 2 times 3, plus 2\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"8 is equal to 8\"></span>. Then, for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x greater than 3\"></span>, the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power\"></span> is greater than the value of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x plus 2\"></span>. So there is a constant, 3, such that when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2\"></span>, but when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than 3\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than 3\"></span>. Choice B is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span>. Choice D is incorrect because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is less than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 raised to the x power is greater than, 2 x plus 2\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x is greater than 3\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959627,"updateDate":1691007959627}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959627, 1691007959627),
    ($SATQ$9b5b23fc$SATQ$, $SATQ$87f878d4-305d-414f-8da8-f430f23c0bfd$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$5fe9082a-ec5b-4b97-be30-3d286a93ff2f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">For <math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is defined as follows:</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;equals <math alttext="201 percent sign"><mrow><mn>201</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following could describe this function?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2d4b4577-9816-4a10-a25c-287b248c3409","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"2e1ade7d-19cd-4603-8a9f-21303a604390","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"e0b84d35-e095-46da-9660-9c4e86e478de","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"6710471c-3121-4ca6-9957-55562039249c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6710471c-3121-4ca6-9957-55562039249c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that for&nbsp;<math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is equal to&nbsp;<math alttext="201 percent sign"><mn>201</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals StartFraction 201 Over 100 EndFraction x"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>201</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>, or <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 2.01 x"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2.01</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, for <math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. This function indicates that as <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases,&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> also increases, which means <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> is an increasing function. Furthermore,&nbsp; <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> increases at a constant rate of <math alttext="2.01"><mn>2.01</mn>
</math> for each increase of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> by <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>. A function with a constant rate of change is linear. Thus, the function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi>
</math> can be described as an increasing linear function.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This could describe the function <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals left parenthesis 2.01 right parenthesis Superscript x"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>2.01</mn></mfenced><mi>x</mi></msup></math>, where <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is equal to&nbsp;<math alttext="201 percent sign"><mn>201</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis x minus 1 right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>, for&nbsp;<math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9b5b23fc","external_id":"87f878d4-305d-414f-8da8-f430f23c0bfd","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"5fe9082a-ec5b-4b97-be30-3d286a93ff2f","uId":"e0717857-0c6f-45e8-ae0f-d9b7c985a8a2","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">For <math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined as follows:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;equals <math alttext=\"201 percent sign\"><mrow><mn>201</mn></mrow><mo>%</mo></math> of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following could describe this function?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2d4b4577-9816-4a10-a25c-287b248c3409","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"2e1ade7d-19cd-4603-8a9f-21303a604390","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Decreasing linear</p>"},{"id":"e0b84d35-e095-46da-9660-9c4e86e478de","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing exponential</p>"},{"id":"6710471c-3121-4ca6-9957-55562039249c","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Increasing linear</p>"}],"keys":["6710471c-3121-4ca6-9957-55562039249c"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that for&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\">